course: dictionary
lesson: 4212
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Each US state has a governor» means a person in charge of a state. Ask yourself: who is in charge here, and of what?
explain: «The school governors met on Tuesday to talk about the new playground.» Here a governor is a volunteer who helps run a school, not a ruler. The word school is the clue. Put your meaning into the sentence to check that it fits.
explain: Informal words change meaning too. «Guv'nor» is an old, friendly word for boss, and the speaker's tone tells you it is not a ruler at all. If the context does not settle it, a dictionary will.
fact: A governor is a person chosen or elected to be in charge of a region, such as a state of the USA.
fact: A school governor is a volunteer who helps run a school.
fact: The governor of a prison or a bank is its head.
fact: A governor-general represents the king or queen in countries like Canada, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: The same word can have different meanings, so look at the words around it to find the right one.
exercise: «Each US state has a governor.» What is a governor here? | A volunteer who helps run a school | A boat on a river | *A person chosen to be in charge of a state | A type of cake
exercise: «The governor of the bank made the decision.» What does governor mean? | A volunteer who reads stories to children | A sweet, sticky drink | *The head of the bank | A sailor on a ship
exercise: Ben's dad calls his boss «guv'nor». What does guv'nor mean? | *Boss | Prisoner | Teacher | Ghost
test: «The school governors chose a new head teacher.» What are school governors? | *Volunteers who help run the school | Children who lead the choir | People who clean the classrooms | Pupils who are head of the class
test: «Pontius Pilate was a Roman governor.» What was a Roman governor? | A soldier who sailed the seas | A kind of road | *A person in charge of a region, ruling for Rome | A coin used in Rome
exam: In «The governor of the prison checked every cell», what does governor mean? | *The head of the prison | A volunteer who helps run a school | A captain of a boat | A kind of cake
